  "title": "elastic-mapping: Add mandatory index_patterns name",
  "description": "ElasticSearch index templates require a index_pattern name that is an\narray of strings:\n\nhttps://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/indices-templates-v1.html\n\nOur current format is the v1 legacy \"_template\" API. The newer\n\"_index_template\" API would also require that key, but also need\nother changes to the structure.\n\nUpdate by adding the name with the value the appropriate array\ncontaining as wildcard the index names that we write in the ek (and\njson) output from tshark.\n\nFix #19657 (combined with fe1217ac75d57b44a3b and 54ebf23913a7637631745)\n\nThere's still some other points raised in that issue, but they're\nduplicates of other issues.",
